    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d206">

                <pb facs="0601" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v04/pg565"/>

                <head>206. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Vietnam<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d206-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1966-08-07T13:57:00-04:00">August 7, 1966,
                            1:57 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>23355. Literally eyes only for Lodge from Rusk. I was most interested in your
                        2818,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d206-f2"/> especially beginning with paragraph
                    four. You should know that we have had some intimation about Thoʼs attitude from
                    an interested Viet Cong source in Europe. Some recent public discussion in Hanoi
                    reflects concern about the solidarity of some of their comrades in the
                    South.</p>
                <p>A defection by some of the key Liberation Front leaders could be worth many
                    battalions to us and could greatly stimulate Chieu Hoi among rank and file. Iʼm
                    sure you know that funds in any amount will be provided if silver bullets will
                    help.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
